            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0190" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/471.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretary of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your Department’s letter of
                    January 10, 1914. relative to payments made by the Chinese Government on account
                    of the Boxer Indemnity for 1913, I have the honor to request that the portion
                    mentioned therein as due the United States, $539,798.06, be retained by your
                    Department, and the amount refundable to China, $543,007.63, be remitted by
                    check, through this Department, to the Charge d’Affaires of China, Washington,
                    D. C.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
